                                                                     ## # Windows BSOD Diagnostic Procedure # ##


                                                          Windows suddenly stops and displays a blue screen with an error code
                                                                     (EXAMPLE:  0x0000007E, 0x0000001E).



                                                       The system may automatically restart or remain on the blue screen until manually rebooted.
                                    A Blue Screen of Death (BSOD) is a critical system error in Windowsthat forces the operating system to stop to prevent further damageto the system.


  # Cause # 
BSODs occur when Windows encounters a critical error it cannot safely recover from. Common causes include:
Faulty or outdated device drivers
Corrupted system files /  Windows updates Errors
Failing hardware (RAM, HDD/SSD, CPU, GPU)
Conflicting software or system misconfiguration





      # Steps / Resolution #
Step 1: Capture Error Info
Note the BSOD error code and message.
Use a camera/screenshot in a lab to document the screen.
If the system auto-restarts, check Event Viewer: System for recent critical errors.
> No critical errors were observed because the system has not experienced a BSOD or significant system failure.

Step 2 – Repair System Files
Run System File Checker to repair corrupted system files:
  - sfc /scannow
  - Run DISM to repair the Windows image:

  - DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth
Update Windows to ensure all patches are installed.


Remove or update any recently installed drivers or software.



