Notes / Lab Takeaways
BSOD error codes provide clues to the root cause; logging and screenshots are critical for analysis.
SFC/DISM repair and driver updates fix many software-related BSODs.
Persistent BSODs often indicate hardware failure; memory dump file analysis pinpoints the problematic module.


    # Why it Work #
This structured approach isolates the cause of a BSOD step by step. Reviewing logs and stop codes identifies failure timing, while SFC and DISM fix common system file issues.
Safe Mode and driver rollback help determine if software or drivers are responsible. Hardware diagnostics check RAM and storage stability. Finally, memory dump analysis of the file with WinDbg pinpoints the likely driver or
module causing the crash. Following these steps ensures both software and hardware issues are systematically addressed.
